    "https://www.bluffton.edu/academiclife/career/Images/Professional-Email-Guide.pdf": {
      "title": "Professional Email Guide",
      "description": " \nProfessional Email Guide  \nHow to write a professional email \nUnderstanding how to write a professional email can help you draft effective \ncommunications for a variety of workplace needs, whether you're interacting with \ncolleagues or customers. Follow these steps to create a thoughtful professional email: \n1. Create an informative subject line \nThe subject line of an email lets its recipients know what to expect before they begin \nreading it and often helps them prioritize the other emails in their inbox. Write a subject \nline that's straightforward and concise so that your intended recipients can understand \nits main purpose quickly. Keeping your subject line succinct can also ensure that your \nrecipients can read it, regardless of the browser they're using. In addition, use engaging \nlanguage to entice them to open your email. If it's appropriate for you to do so, consider \npersonalizing your subject line by including their name in it.  \n2. Provide a polite greeting \nYou can begin most professional emails with \"Dear\" or \"Hello.\" If you're writing to a \ncolleague who you have a close working relationship with, it's beneficial to include their \nfirst name in your greeting. If you're addressing your email to a direct supervisor or \nmanager, make sure you include both their first and last name, along with the \nappropriate honorific. When addressing clients or customers, you may use language \nthat's less formal, depending on your employer's requirements.  \n3. Address the purpose of your email  \nState the purpose of the email in the first sentence below your greeting and try to keep \nyour copy as brief as possible. This ensures that you're honoring your recipient's time \nand providing them with the information they need. Consider using a bulleted or \nnumbered list to help organize the information if there are several points you want to \naddress. Make sure you structure your email in a way that communicates its importance \nto the recipient clearly and you include proof for any claims you choose to make.  \n \n \n \n \n4. Include a clear call to action \nIf you want the recipient to do something in response to your email, specify what this is. \nIn addition, include details on how you want them to respond if you're expecting a reply. \nLet them know if there's a deadline you want them to be aware of and the level of \nurgency in responding to your email. Be sure to attach any additional information that \nmight be necessary for them to access, such as important files or documents and let \nthem know what these are in your call to action.  \n5. Close with your contact information \nConclude the letter with your name, job title and contact information. This information \nmay include your phone number, website and any additional information that you think \nmay be important for your recipients to contact you. You may also provide your address, \nparticularly if you want the recipient to send you physical documents or products. Even \nthough recipients can see your email address when you email them, it's also beneficial \nto include it in your contact information to highlight your professionalism. \n______________________________________________________________________\n______________ \nIndeed Editorial Team. (2026, June 15). How to write a professional email (with templates). Indeed. \nhttps://www.indeed.com/career-advice/career-development/how-to-write-professional-email-with-\ntemplates [indeed.com] \n "
    },
    "https://a.cms.omniupdate.com/11/?skin=oucampus&account=bluffton&site=www-redesign&action=de&path=/academiclife/career/index.pcf": {
      "title": "Modern Campus CMS",
      "description": "Log In - Modern Campus CMS Modern Campus CMS Logo Modern Campus CMS Help Support Community Feedback Log in to your account Username LOGIN Reset Password Change Password Please enter a new password for user in account . New Password Reset Cancel System Announcements We're sorry; the system could not log you in. The authentication server returned the following error message: Reset Password Password reset instructions will be emailed to the address entered below. Username SUBMIT Back to Login Page Reset Password Your request was successfull. You will receive an email containing a link to reset your password. Back to Login Page Javascript Disabled Modern Campus CMS requires Javascript. Please enable Javascript in your browser settings."
    }
